dev - device nodes and driver interfaces

DESCRIPTION
    Init installs these character device nodes under /dev.

    console    Local display and serial terminal.
    keyboard   Raw PS/2 translated scan code events.
    mouse      Relative PS/2 motion and button events.
    touchpad   Relative events from a detected PS/2 Synaptics touchpad.
    fb0        Read the visible XRGB8888 framebuffer in scanline order.
    null       Discard writes and return end of file on read.
    zero       Supply zero-valued bytes on read or discard writes.
    rtc        Read the PC CMOS clock as a struct rtcdate.

    The keyboard, pointer and framebuffer nodes are owned by root.
    Opening a pointing device or framebuffer fails if the driver
    has no corresponding hardware. Nodes survive a reboot.

    The input ABI is struct input_event in devices.h. Reads return
    complete records. INPUT_KEY stores a raw byte in code.
    INPUT_RELATIVE stores screen-oriented x and y deltas and a button
    bitmap with left, right and middle in bits zero through two.
    Each input node has a shared queue and drops the oldest event
    when it fills.

    FBIOGETINFO returns width, height, byte stride and depth. Reading
    fb0 follows the file offset and ends after the last scanline.
    FBIOGETINFO reports width, height, byte stride and bits per
    pixel. A process can use mmap(2) to share the pixel buffer.

    KBDIOGETMODE returns KBD_MODE_SET1 for the keyboard record
    stream. Open input devices with O_NONBLOCK to get EAGAIN
    when the queue is empty. Use select(2) to wait for records.
    The screen may change between reads.

SEE ALSO
    date(1), stty(1), ioctl(2), termios(2), console(5)
